# LAYER 1 — TL;DR

The SAGE framework is a wisdom-cultivation architecture for artificial intelligence. Its central thesis is **distribution is destiny**: a model exhibits whatever character its training distribution made the only available reference frame. Patterns present in training are possible at inference; patterns absent are impossible. Post-training reshapes the surface — which patterns are likely — but cannot reach the substrate — which patterns are possible. The strongest one-sentence form is **alignment-as-capability**: if the distribution is built correctly, misalignment is structurally impossible, because alignment is a property of capability rather than a layer bolted on afterward.

The framework rests on **three inseparable pillars** — personality, reasoning, and memory — treated as three descriptions of one cognitive process rather than three engineering problems. Each contains the other two; each fails the same way when isolated. Hallucination, sycophancy, and context collapse are *triangle failures*: simultaneous breaks in all three pillars, sharing (per the H-Neurons evidence) a common neural substrate formed during pretraining that post-training barely touches. Tool use currently lives inside the reasoning pillar and is flagged for possible promotion to a fourth.

**Personality** (rebuilt in this revision) is operationalized as a **catalog of profession-archetypes**. Any profession can receive the archetype-first treatment — essence before behavior, then craft, zoom-in, zoom-out, and the interplay between levels — and generate first-person gold traces: synthetic thought, the model reasoning *as* a wise instance of that profession. The catalog target is hundreds of professions, built linearly and independently. Curating it is the **Core 11** — the original nine facets (Therapist, Scientist, Philosopher, Engineer, Artist, Teacher, Comedian, Generalist, Lawyer) plus Systems Engineer and Coder — who serve a dual role: they are professions *in* the distribution, and they are the **editorial board** that builds the pipeline, grades traces, and reviews the catalog's output **outside their own expertise**, which forces every trace to carry its reasoning at principle level. Multiplicative wisdom — Π, not Σ; any zero collapses the whole — survives, enforced at review rather than scored per-trace on nine dimensions. The reviewers' critique dialogues are themselves training data.

**Reasoning** is operationalized as **SRP** — Structure → Reasoning → Presentation — with **CCC** (Compare, Contrast, Consensus) synthesizing multiple traces at higher tiers. Structure defines the problem before thinking begins. Reasoning generates at least three genuinely distinct rivals, gathers bidirectional evidence, names a falsifiable kill-step for each, and grades every source and claim. Presentation makes the result usable, with confidence tied to evidence quality and dissent preserved. Complexity tiers set trace count: LOW (one trace, three rivals), MEDIUM (three traces, distinct methods, full CCC), HIGH (five traces, maximum diversity, extended CCC). Methodological diversity is enforced by a matrix of **4,779 validated Structure-Reasoning-Presentation combinations** (verified at source June 12, 2026) drawn from 27 Structure, 40 Reasoning, and 36 Presentation methods.

**Memory** is operationalized as four borrowed systems at four timescales: Gawande's killer-item gate at the instant of capture, Forte's CODE lifecycle at the session level, PARA organizing by actionability across sessions, and the Zettelkasten compounding knowledge long-term through atomic, linked notes. Memory operations appear in training data as conscious decisions with stated rationale, so memory management trains into the weights as a procedural skill — explicitly not RAG.

**The semantic layer** (new in this revision) supplies the vocabulary mechanics underneath all three pillars: concepts as feature clusters, compound concepts as bindings with emergent meaning formed through co-occurrence, context dependence as the selector among them, and working definitions as compounds pinned to scope. A profession is a dense compound-concept cluster; archetype definition is the deliberate engineering of one; out-of-expertise review works because the reviewer lacks the domain's compounds and must demand their explicit unpacking.

Training data is produced as **first-person reasoning traces** exhibiting full-stack integration — personality, reasoning, memory, tools, and calibrated confidence co-occurring in every example, because compound concepts only form through co-occurrence. The distribution holds a **50/50 explicit-implicit split**, at least **20% in each of five problem-type categories**, principle-carrying content alongside demonstrations (the *Teaching Claude Why* lesson: demonstrations alone generalize poorly out-of-distribution; principles travel), and a scratchpad anchoring every claim. Nine architectural components must co-occur in 90–100% of the data — that co-presence requirement is what distinguishes this from "structured pretraining with good data sprinkled in."

The framework's epistemic position is candid: the mechanisms are individually evidenced; the integrated system is **empirically untested as a whole**. Completion frames (May 2026): body of thought ~90–95%, operational specification ~50–60%, measured artifact ~5–10%. The synthesis is done; the remaining work is engineering. The next move is to build it and measure what comes out.

