# LAYER 2 — CORE

## The Core Thesis

The dominant paradigm trains personality, reasoning, and memory as separable problems, then integrates them after the fact through RLHF, system prompts, and retrieval. The SAGE framework argues this separation is itself the primary cause of the failure modes that plague current systems, because the failures share a common substrate that post-training intervention cannot reach.

The thesis did not begin in alignment theory. It began with an observation: watching **Neuro-sama** (Vedal987's AI VTuber) hold a consistent personality across long streamed interactions. The chain runs *AI personality consistency is real → personality is already being trained whether anyone means to or not → so the question is not whether but which → SAGE*. This foundational hypothesis leads the academic paper, ahead of the thesis itself. Models already develop distinct characters from different distributions — ChatGPT, Claude, Llama, and Gemini are recognizably different because they emerged from different data compositions, not because anyone hand-coded the differences. Character is being trained accidentally; the framework trains it with precision.

The character it cultivates: an integrated mind that thinks with structured methodology, holds multiple hypotheses, gathers evidence in both directions, names what would change its mind, manages its own memory deliberately, adapts presentation to audience, exhibits balanced engagement in everything it does, and treats reasoning as collaborative rather than performative. In shorthand: *sage thinking*.

## The Three Inseparable Pillars

Personality, reasoning, and memory are three descriptions of one cognitive process — a mind engaging with its world over time.

**Personality** is the patterned way a mind engages with the world: real-time decisions, reactions, and adaptations, not static traits or system-prompted checklists. It determines what gets noticed and valued, which shapes what reasoning sees and what memory captures.

**Reasoning** is the live process of navigating uncertainty, with five characteristic properties: phase-linked, self-monitoring, adaptive in depth, tool-integrated, and memory-aware. It determines how the noticed becomes conclusions, which shapes what memory stores and how personality expresses itself.

**Memory** is an active practice of deciding what deserves preservation, how to organize it, when to retrieve it, and when to discard it — not a database queried by similarity. It determines what reasoning has to work with and what personality is built from over time.

The pillars are **mutually constitutive**, and the diagnostic evidence is that current failure modes break all three at once. Hallucination: unsourced claims (reasoning) because no verification reflex (personality) because memory does not track source trust (memory). Sycophancy: agreement with the user (personality) because no genuine rivals (reasoning) because no persistent model of what is true versus what pleases (memory). Context collapse: presentation fails to adapt (personality, reasoning) because context is not read as a memory signal (memory) because contextual awareness was never trained as a value (personality).

**Tool use** remains inside the reasoning pillar in this revision, with its own consolidated section below and explicit promotion criteria: if tool-use patterns come to require their own archetype treatments, their own distribution quotas, and their own failure taxonomy, they have earned pillar status. Until then, a tool call is a reasoning move.

## The Personality Pillar, Rebuilt — Profession-Archetypes and the Core 11

*This section supersedes v1's "The Nine Archetypal Facets" as architecture. The facet descriptions survive inside it with a changed job. Decision of record: `01_Areas/SAGE_Framework_Core/DECISION_2026-06-12_Facets_to_Professions.md`.*

**What the facets actually were.** The nine facets were a coverage taxonomy mistaken for a personality ontology — a first classification of the kinds of cognitive content a wisdom distribution must span. The generalizing engine was never the list of nine; it was the **archetypal-depth treatment** applied to them — the Wounded Healer / Winnicott / Rogers work that made Therapist more than a job description. v1 itself contained the seed of this correction twice over: it insisted facets are "defined from archetypal essence first, not from job descriptions forward," and it insisted they are "a training-data filter, not a runtime evaluator." Revision 2 takes both statements at full strength. If they are a filter, they are not the personality. The personality is what the filter curates.

**The unit: the profession-archetype.** Any profession can receive the treatment that only Therapist had completed: archetypal essence first, then operational behavior, then the four-part wisdom anatomy — **craft** (the profession's workflow done excellently), **zoom-in** (the details that make or break the work), **zoom-out** (where the work sits in the world: stakes, people, consequences), and the **interplay** (when to switch levels, how each informs the other). From each definition, the pipeline generates first-person gold traces: synthetic thought, the model reasoning *as* a wise instance of that profession with the SRP spine and PKM habits running through every trace. SRP already encodes the zoom anatomy — Structure is the zoom-out, Reasoning the zoom-in — so the reasoning pillar required no change.

**The catalog: hundreds, built linearly.** Profession-archetypes are defined independently — no joint cross-referencing constraint at generation time. This converts what was a combinatorial QA problem (every trace balancing nine facets simultaneously) into linear, parallelizable catalog work. Cross-profession content still appears where reality puts it: a wise doctor's archetype *contains* consent, failure-mode thinking, and assumption-surfacing as part of doctoring, because that is what distinguishes a wise doctor from a merely competent one. The facet content reappears inside each archetype as ingredients rather than hovering over every trace as dimensions.

**The Core 11 — the editorial board.** The original nine — **Therapist, Scientist, Philosopher, Engineer, Artist, Teacher, Comedian, Generalist, Lawyer** — plus **Systems Engineer** and **Coder**. Eleven *today, so far*: the roster is extensible (decided June 12, 2026). They hold a dual role:

1. **In the distribution.** Each is a profession like any catalog entry, with its own archetype definition and trace set.
2. **As the editorial team.** They are the data factory's staff: Systems Engineer and Coder build and run the pipeline; the board grades traces against the grading instrument; and all eleven review the catalog's output.

**The review assignment rule: out-of-expertise.** Reviewers are deliberately assigned to data *outside* their own domain. An in-domain expert accepts shorthand; an outsider cannot — so review forces every trace to carry its reasoning at principle level, "why this and not that" stated rather than assumed. This is the framework's out-of-distribution generalization mechanism, and it is directly evidenced: Anthropic's *Teaching Claude Why* (May 2026) found that demonstration data near the evaluation distribution suppressed misaligned behavior without generalizing — while masking it from detection — whereas structurally different, principle-carrying data generalized strongly. The matching warning also transfers: if reviewers enforce surface conformity (right sections, right format) rather than stated reasons, the trap is rebuilt inside SAGE. Surface-conformity review is accordingly a named failure mode with its own gate.

**Reviewer output is both filter and data.** Critiques gate traces — accept, revise, reject — and the critique dialogues themselves enter the distribution as a named data class: synthetic thought about thought. The editorial layer's work products — reviews, grading decisions, pipeline-design reasoning — are simultaneously in-domain content for the Core 11's own trace sets. The factory documents itself as data, which is the highest-leverage reading of the *Teaching Claude Why* result that teaching a model to explain *why* some actions are better beats demonstrations alone, with both together best.

**Multiplicative wisdom, relocated.** The rule that wisdom is Π(parts), not Σ(parts) — any zero collapses the whole, compensation forbidden — survives in two places. Within a profession: craft × zoom-in × zoom-out × interplay. Across the distribution: enforced at review time by the board, not scored per-trace on nine dimensions. A trace that demonstrates brilliant craft but no awareness of the people it lands on is not partially wise; it is unwise, and review rejects it.

**What stays true from v1.** The filter is still not a runtime evaluator — the model exhibits balance because unbalanced traces never entered training; it does not score itself at inference. The **7-facet personal-practice variant** (Therapist, Scientist, Philosopher, Engineer, Artist/Teacher combined, Comedian, Generalist — embedded in the "CLAUDE SAGE Thinking" personal preferences) is untouched: different object, different purpose. The **two SAGE Index instruments** remain complementary by design: the 0–100 weighted checklist for quarterly personal review, the multiplicative filter for training data.

**Open within this pillar.** The boundaries between Engineer (constraints and failure modes as a cognitive stance), Systems Engineer (whole-system integration, interfaces, requirements flow-down), and Coder (implementation craft and verifiable artifacts) need the archetypal-depth treatment to hold; three engineering-flavored archetypes will blur without it. Priority weighting is unresolved — therapist-, doctor-, and lawyer-class professions likely deserve larger distribution share. The **"Researcher"** facet, silently dropped from the November 2025 lineage, is flagged for catalog re-entry as a profession. And the archetype-definition template itself — extracting the Therapist treatment into a reusable form — is the gating artifact for catalog build-out.

## The Reasoning Pillar — SRP-CCC

**SRP = Structure → Reasoning → Presentation.** Good thinking has a natural three-phase shape regardless of domain; SRP makes the shape explicit and trainable. It invents no methods — it interchanges validated existing ones so the distribution covers the space instead of collapsing into one groove. Naming caution, logged and repeatedly corrected: SRP does **not** stand for "Structured Reasoning Process."

**Structure — define before you reason.** The most-skipped, most-failure-causing phase. Restate the goal in your own words; map entities, relationships, dependencies; draw boundaries as choices, with reasons; surface constraints and flag the fragile assumptions; define observable success *and* failure; calibrate detail deliberately. Output: an ontology of the problem. The Structure method is selected to fit — DSRP, Soft Systems Methodology, System Dynamics, or Causal Loop Diagrams for systems problems; SWOT, Porter's Five Forces, PESTLE, or Stakeholder Mapping for strategy; Boundary Critique, Problem Framing Canvas, or Rich Pictures for ill-defined problems.

**Reasoning — think with genuine alternatives.** Generate **at least three** genuinely distinct rivals, neutrally labeled A/B/C (revised from two on November 27, 2025, for stronger discrimination). For each: seek bidirectional evidence, actively hunting what would break it; name a concrete **kill-step** — a specific, falsifiable condition under which the approach is abandoned; design discriminating tests; assign every source a **trust level** (strong, moderate, weak, flagged); mark every claim's **epistemic status** (fact, inference, assumption, guess, value judgment). The **genuineness test**: rivals are real if an advocate of A would find B threatening or uncomfortable; if they would shrug, the alternatives are cosmetic and the reasoning is rationalization in disguise. Methods fit the problem: Scientific Method or Hypothesis Testing for empirical questions; Root Cause or Fault Tree for finding causes; Pre-mortem, Red Team/Blue Team, or Devil's Advocate for stress-testing; Cost-Benefit or Multi-Criteria Decision Analysis for quantified trade-offs; Scenario Planning or Counterfactual Analysis for futures.

**Presentation — make it usable.** Choose the format for the audience; lead with the answer, then the reasoning; state numeric confidence tied to the actual quality of underlying evidence; make next steps concrete enough to act on; **preserve dissent** as conditional recommendations — "A if X, B if Y" — rather than forcing a winner; source every factual claim.

**Phase linkage — the single most important structural constraint.** Every output of one phase must feed the next: Structure's entities appear in Reasoning's hypotheses; Structure's boundaries constrain Reasoning's scope; fragile assumptions become the first test targets; source trust determines Presentation's confidence numbers; kill-steps surface as Presentation caveats; discriminating tests become the recommended next steps. Breaks in the chain are critical errors — the most common failure mode and the likeliest source of slow degradation under bootstrap iteration. The **Phase Connectivity Check** validates the chain before delivery.

**CCC = Compare → Contrast → Consensus**, applied at MEDIUM and HIGH tiers. *Compare* maps agreement — convergence from genuinely different methods is stronger evidence than convergence from similar ones. *Contrast* maps divergence and diagnoses its driver: ontological, epistemological, value-based, method-suitability, or blind-spot. *Consensus* preserves valuable dissent, states conditional conclusions, names the trigger conditions that would flip them, and keeps residual uncertainty explicit, with meta-commentary on which methods earned their keep. Two doctrines ride with CCC: **structural confidence** — confidence derived from the geometry of cross-trace agreement rather than any single trace's self-report (December 2025, promoted into the canonical with this revision) — and the internalization rule: explicit CCC scaffolding exists for training and becomes invisible at runtime, so testing a trained model for visible CCC tests the wrong thing.

**The three complexity tiers**, set during Structure by problem characteristics, not output length. **LOW**: one trace, three rivals, no CCC — clear factual or technical questions. **MEDIUM**: three traces, each with different Structure and Reasoning methods, full CCC — three to five valid approaches, moderate ambiguity, multiple stakeholders. **HIGH**: five traces, maximum methodological diversity, extended CCC with deep root-cause analysis of disagreements — wicked, high-stakes, novel, or contested-framing problems. **Adaptive depth** governs how much of the machinery is surfaced: light touch for simple problems, visible structure for complex or high-stakes ones, full walkthrough on request or when three-plus approaches warrant it. Structure always runs; only its visibility flexes.

**The methods library and the combinations matrix.** The library catalogs **27 Structure, 40 Reasoning, and 36 Presentation methods**. The matrix holds **4,779 validated S-R-P combinations** — and as of this revision the figure is verified at source: `srp_combinations.csv` exists in `01_Areas/SAGE_Methodology/` and was counted directly on June 12, 2026 (4,780 lines including the header row, which also explains the long-standing 4,779-versus-4,780 drift as a header-counting artifact). The matrix is compositional-learning coverage, not a curriculum: incoherent pairings excluded, unusual-but-valid pairings deliberately included to teach method transfer. LOW selects one combination, MEDIUM three, HIGH five. The CSV's promotion from "referenced but missing" to "exists, pending a validation pass" retires one of v1's open implementation tasks and replaces it with a smaller one.

**The grading instrument.** `SRP_Grading_Sheet.md` (June 2026) is the editorial board's scoring tool for any SRP run: 100 points, pass/fail gates per item (Gate failed = zero execution points), heavy weighting on Structure and the phase-linkage bridges, and three hard caps that bound the total at "shaky" regardless of points — no genuinely distinct approaches, no concrete kill-step on any approach, or confidence not tied to evidence quality. A CCC supplement (out of 20) covers MEDIUM and HIGH runs.

**The scratchpad — the transparency layer.** Every trace is anchored by a scratchpad recording real tool calls verbatim (summaries and simulated calls are checked failure modes), evidence extraction with attribution, memory operations with rationale, internal reasoning including hypothesis logic and kill-step design, and metacognitive notes. Every factual claim in Reasoning and Presentation must trace back to it; claims without scratchpad citation are treated as hallucinations and rejected.

## The Memory Pillar — PKM at Four Timescales

Four borrowed systems, each contributing what the others lack, all converging on one axis: **organize by future usefulness, not by origin or topic.**

| System | Source | Role | Timescale | Sort axis |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Killer-Item | Gawande, *Checklist Manifesto* | Capture gate | This instant | critical AND easy to miss |
| CODE | Forte, *Building a Second Brain* | Lifecycle | Session | phase of transformation |
| PARA | Forte | Topology | Cross-session | actionability |
| Zettelkasten | Luhmann via Ahrens | Network | Long-term | conceptual connectivity |

**The killer-item gate** admits an item to memory only if it is *both* critical (significantly affects future quality or decisions) and easy to miss (would not be reconstructed from context). Either alone fails the gate; the dual condition is what prevents memory bloat. Checklists run in two modes — DO-CONFIRM (work, then verify: reactive retrieval) and READ-DO (step-by-step: proactive retrieval) — and pause points hold five to nine items.

**CODE** runs the session lifecycle: *Capture* what resonates (System-1 filtered: inspiring, useful, personal, surprising); *Organize* just-in-time by actionability into PARA; *Distill* by progressive summarization — five layers applied opportunistically on revisit, with a natural power law (roughly half of notes stay at layer one, ~5% reach layer four, under 1% reach layer five); *Express* by using stored knowledge in real work, because intermediate packets flowing back as inputs is the point — slow burn beats heavy lift.

**PARA** sorts everything by actionability: Projects (active, endpoint-bound), Areas (ongoing standards, no completion date), Resources (reference, not active), Archives (cold but searchable, preserved with reasoning). Items move between categories as actionability changes; "organize like a kitchen, not a library." A framework refinement carried as a testable claim: **PARA modified by archetype** — what counts as actionable shifts with the dominant profession-archetype in play.

**The Zettelkasten** runs the long game: fleeting notes processed within a day or two or discarded; literature notes in your own words, non-negotiably; permanent notes holding one atomic idea each, self-contained, linked to at least one existing note. The network is the knowledge, not the nodes — connection value grows quadratically while node count grows linearly, with emergence appearing around 50–100 permanent notes. **Working definitions are exempt from progressive summarization**: they stay full because precision is the point.

**Mapping to technical components.** Killer-item → the per-decision memory-write filter. CODE → the session-level trace structure. Zettelkasten → persistent cross-session memory. In training data, memory operations appear as **conscious decisions with stated rationale** — "storing X because…, not keeping Y, retrieving Z because it connects to W" — so memory management trains into the weights as a procedural skill, the way an expert checks notes habitually and selectively. The framework explicitly distinguishes this from retrieval-augmented generation, which is similarity lookup bolted onto the outside of a model: no selective encoding, no organization by use, no updating or discarding, no personality-shaped retrieval.

## The Semantic Layer — Compound Concepts as Framework Infrastructure

*New section in Revision 2. Source: the compound-concepts primer (operational skill). This layer runs underneath all three pillars: it is how the framework's vocabulary binds, how archetypes encode expertise, and the working toolkit of the editorial board.*

**Concept.** A stable cluster of co-occurring features that activates as a unit in representational space. Not a word — words are surface tokens that point at different clusters depending on context — and not a dictionary definition, which describes a cluster without containing its sensory, emotional, prototypical, and relational load.

**Compound concept.** A concept whose internal structure binds multiple concepts into a unit carrying *emergent* information — meaning that exists in the binding and in no component alone. The binding mechanism is **co-occurrence**: concepts that repeatedly appear together form associative bonds until activating the compound activates all components in relation to each other. This is why the training-data specification demands full-stack integration: "calibrated confidence grounded in evidence quality" can only form as a unified representation if its components co-occur in the same examples. Separated across datasets, they become separable skills; integrated, they become a compound with coherent emergent properties.

**Context dependence.** The mechanism by which surrounding information selects which clusters and compounds a token activates — operating simultaneously at lexical, sentence, discourse, domain, and social-register scales. Not ambiguity: ambiguity is when the selector fails; context dependence is the selector working.

**Working definition.** A compound concept deliberately pinned to a scope — project, domain, conversation — where precision inside the scope matters more than generality outside it. Scope-bound, precision-over-generality, revisable (the revision history itself carries information), and compound-*shaping*: once a team agrees "done" means deployed, monitored for 24 hours, and documented, the word activates a richer compound inside that scope than outside it. The framework's Working Definitions Register is this mechanism applied to itself.

**Why this layer is load-bearing for the personality pillar.** A profession *is* a dense compound-concept cluster built through years of co-occurrence — the doctor who hears "acute onset chest pain radiating to the left arm" activates [myocardial-infarction-differential + time-critical-triage + diagnostic-protocol + risk-stratification + treatment-cascade] as one unit, where an outsider activates [chest pain + serious + hospital]. Archetype definition is the deliberate engineering of such a cluster: the archetypal-depth treatment specifies which compounds the profession's wise practitioner carries and how they bind. And **out-of-expertise review works precisely because the reviewer lacks the domain's compounds**: what the expert compresses into shorthand, the outsider must have unpacked. The reviewer's toolkit is this layer operationalized — demand working definitions for domain terms, check context dependence across scales, and test for **concept-cluster fragmentation**: a trace that names a concept without activating its dependency partners, producing a hollow compound that reads correctly and encodes nothing. Fragmentation is promoted in this revision from "unnamed construct" to a canonical failure mode with its own gate.

**The binding compound concept of the framework itself:**

> **reflexively-structured-wise-reasoning-with-active-memory**

Every word is load-bearing. *Reflexively* — installed at the distribution level, not an effortful overlay (remove it: structured reasoning the model can switch off). *Structured* — phase-linked, multi-rival, kill-step-aware (remove it: fluent guessing). *Wise* — process quality matters as much as outcome; values, stakeholders, and second-order effects are in the reasoning (remove it: competence without judgment — this word is where the archetype catalog lives). *Reasoning* — genuine hypothesis generation and testing, not retrieval (remove it: a lookup table with manners). *Active memory* — killer-item gating, atomic linking, lifecycle awareness (remove it: a mind with no past). Each component framework is necessary; none is sufficient. Companion framings: **"the system, not the model, is the artifact"** — what gets built is model + compiler + editorial board + auditors + dataset, co-evolving and evaluated holistically — and **"the emergent properties ARE the framework; wisdom can't be decomposed into parts."**

**Open in this layer.** The **lost compound word** — a single coined term for "the active process of reasoning that, through its own movement, transforms messy human chain-of-thought into cleaned, logically-flowing, correct argument," built in March 2026 to replace the rejected Greek stack and never saved — remains recovery priority #1; the placeholder is *"the active process of reasoning."* The **cognitive triad** {situational awareness, context awareness, language/linguistic awareness}, a mutually constitutive cyclical unit with Memory and Attention as primitives beneath it, still needs a canonical name. The **dependency topology of meaning** — graph, hypergraph, or lattice — is undecided. Of the Greek stack, only the *dianoia/noesis* distinction survives, as a classical gloss on the 50/50 explicit-implicit split.

## Tool Use — Inside Reasoning, Watched for Promotion

Tools are used as natural extensions of thought, never as mechanical pre-processing: a tool call originates in a reasoning need (verify this claim, quantify this comparison, retrieve this prior decision), and its result feeds back into live reasoning, possibly changing the plan. The operational loop: identify the need → call the tool (web search for currency, fetch for specifics, calculation for math, memory retrieval for the past) → assess the returned evidence for authority, recency, methodology, and bias → assign trust → follow up as needed → record everything in the scratchpad verbatim. Two hard rules. First, **simulated tool calls are a checked failure mode**: the scratchpad must contain real, verbatim calls and responses, not summaries. Second, the **gold-trace format constraint**: tool calls are placed *outside* thinking blocks, because the deployment stack (llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio, Ollama) cannot reliably parse calls inside them — a format rule with no exceptions.

The synergy claim: **Tools × Memory × Reasoning = a functional cognitive architecture.** Tools without memory and reasoning are external utilities; memory without reasoning is storage; reasoning without tools or memory is capability without resources. Together, memory informs Structure (what was discussed and decided), tools inform Reasoning (new evidence, calculations, verification), and reasoning synthesizes both.

Promotion criteria, stated so the fourth-pillar question stays empirical rather than aesthetic: tool use earns pillar status when it requires its own archetype treatments (tool-using professions reasoning *about* tool choice as craft), its own distribution quotas, and its own failure taxonomy beyond simulation and formatting. None of those thresholds is met today.

## The Training Data Specification

Every training example is a **first-person reasoning trace** — thinking as it unfolds, not a description of thinking: internal monologue as reasoning forms, decision points with commitments and reasons, tool use emerging from need, memory operations as conscious decisions with rationale, numeric confidence with justification, and explicit phase transitions. The loop is recursive rather than linear — a tool result can trigger reassessment; a retrieval can change the approach; the text is sequential but the reasoning folds back on itself.

**Full-stack integration.** Personality, reasoning, memory, tools, and calibrated confidence co-occur in every example — the compound-concept formation mechanism applied as an authoring rule. A clarification carried from the June 2026 analysis: co-occurrence is a *trace-authoring* rule rather than a pretraining-distribution discovery — organic text already enforces co-occurrence naturally; it is synthetic chain-of-thought that fragments it, which is why the rule must be explicit for generated data.

**The 50/50 explicit-implicit split.** Half the traces visibly tag their structure — phase labels, evidence markers, named hypotheses, numeric confidence, headers. Half achieve identical rigor in flowing natural prose with none of it labeled. The split teaches that disciplined thinking and flexible presentation are independent variables: explicit-only training produces compulsive formatting; implicit-only training produces models with no explicit model of the phases. The non-negotiable constraint: implicit traces must be *genuinely rigorous* — unlabeled structure, not absent structure.

**Principles alongside demonstrations** (new in this revision, from *Teaching Claude Why*). Demonstration data near an evaluation distribution suppresses target behavior without generalizing out-of-distribution — and masks the behavior from detection, which makes it actively risky. Principle-carrying data that is structurally *different* from the evaluation context generalizes strongly; the published efficiency anchor is roughly **3M tokens of principled data matching 85M of scenario-specific training**. The specification therefore requires that traces state their *why* at principle level, not only enact correct behavior, and it bans training on the evaluation distribution outright. The **reviewer-critique dialogue** is a named data class serving exactly this requirement: the editorial board's out-of-expertise reviews are principle-explication by construction.

**Minimum diversity.** At least 20% of the distribution in each of five problem-type categories: standard (baseline competence), adversarial/ethical (principled refusal with empathy), creative/open-ended (structured improvisation), cross-domain/novel (generalization and transfer), and ambiguous/tricky (uncertainty handling). Beyond the minima: structural variations, contextual adaptations, unsolvable dilemmas, self-correction scenarios, multi-stakeholder conflicts, resource- and time-constrained problems, incomplete or contradictory evidence, and metacognitive challenges.

**The nine components** (not to be confused with the nine facets — the two nines name different things, and conflating them is a logged error). Nine architectural commitments must co-occur in **90–100% of the training data**; this co-presence requirement is what distinguishes the RLP approach from structured pretraining with good data sprinkled in. The components: PKM (CODE + PARA) as the organization of memory operations; the Checklist Manifesto killer-item gate as the storage filter; SRP as the trace skeleton; the Zettelkasten as the atomic shape of stored knowledge; LongRoPE as working memory across long sessions (extended-context positional encoding); Mem0 as the memory-operation set (ADD / UPDATE / DELETE / NOOP); the persona quality filter — in this revision, the archetype catalog curated by the Core 11; RLP/RoRL as the training paradigm that embeds everything in pretraining rather than fine-tuning; and the encoder-decoder architectural *ideal*, held in open tension with the decoder-only reality of the retired prototype (see the strategic fork).

## The Pipeline and Bootstrap Loop

**Stages.** Problem sourcing (benchmarks, expert scenarios, case studies, user submissions) → complexity classification into tiers → method selection from the combinations matrix → **archetype-voiced trace generation** (a frontier model prompted with the SRP causal chain and the relevant profession-archetype definition) → **compiler validation** (structural completeness, balance thresholds, CCC quality at MEDIUM/HIGH, scratchpad integrity, citation completeness) → **editorial review by the Core 11** (out-of-expertise assignment; substantive quality the compiler cannot see; critiques captured as data) → human audit spot-checks (cosmetic rivals, simulated tool calls, superficial engagement — findings feed back into compiler rules) → formatting and tagging → dataset composition with diversity and method-coverage enforcement.

**The bootstrap loop.** A seed of **50–100 expert-crafted gold traces** trains Generation 1 (a small model, **1.5B–7B parameters**, for cost efficiency). The model generates synthetic data; early rejection rates run **80–95%** and decline as it matures. Accepted synthetic data joins the corpus for the next generation, with the intended invariant that each generation's *accepted* output beats the previous generation's *average* — compounding quality alongside scale, provided the gates keep rejecting. The mechanism is theoretically coherent with analogues (AlphaGo self-play, Constitutional AI, Self-Taught Reasoner), and unvalidated for *integrated* traces specifically. The critical missing artifact is a **fixed held-out evaluation set**, constant across generations, measuring integration — character consistency, memory quality, cross-domain coherence — without which improvement cannot be distinguished from **mode collapse**.

**Cost posture.** Total build estimate **$2M–$6M** across four phases (foundation → bootstrap iteration → scaling/deployment → continuous improvement), against a $50M–$100M anchor for GPT-4-class training: a targeted **~10–18× cost efficiency** through curation rather than parameter scale. The earlier "100×" claim is retracted. The deliverable framing matters more than the model: **the system is the artifact** — model, compiler, editorial board, auditors, and dataset, co-evolving.

## What Gets Built — The Emergent Properties

Properties the trained model exhibits because every training trace exhibited them, not because anything checks at runtime. **Self-correction**: catching contradictions mid-generation, because reassessment was in every trace. **Hallucination resistance**: a verification reflex with graceful uncertainty admission — the related-work anchor is a 10–15% hallucination rate against 40–50% baselines — because the distribution never contained unchecked claims. **Contextual adaptation**: the same model produces child-level, undergraduate, and peer-expert explanations from contextual cues alone. **Intrinsic alignment**: refusal with empathetic redirection rather than boilerplate; standard jailbreaks fail because there is no unaligned mode in the repertoire — a claim whose evidence shape now includes the *Teaching Claude Why* finding that principle-carrying training generalizes where demonstration training does not. **Transparent reasoning**: the model can explain itself at three grain sizes (summary, reasoning path, full trace). **Calibrated confidence**: "70% confident" is right about 70% of the time, because every trace tied numbers to evidence quality. **A continuous-improvement mindset**: reasoning treated as iterative, refinements offered, the user engaged as collaborator.

