# LAYER 3 — DEEP

## Research Foundations and the Reading List

**Five convergent empirical lines** (the academic backbone, carried from v1 with citations intact):

**1. Pretraining-distribution primacy.** LIMA (Zhou et al., 2023): a 65B LLaMA fine-tuned on 1,000 curated examples, no RLHF, preferred over RLHF-trained DaVinci003 in 65% of comparisons and matching GPT-4 in 43%. Lin et al. (2024): over 92% of aligned-model tokens already sit in the base model's top-3; only 5–8% of positions shift meaningfully, mostly stylistic markers — post-training selects from the distribution rather than adding to it. Phi-1 (1.3B parameters, 7B "textbook-quality" tokens): 50.6% HumanEval, competitive with models trained on 10–100× more data; Phi-2 beat RLHF-aligned models on toxicity purely through curation. DoReMi (Xie et al., 2023): mixture-proportion optimization alone gained 6.5 points and reached baseline with 2.6× fewer steps.

**2. Shallowness of current alignment.** Qi et al. (2025): safety alignment concentrates in the first few output tokens. Arditi et al. (2024): refusal is mediated by a single residual-stream direction; ablate it and refusal disables. Young (2025): a proof that gradient-based alignment receives zero signal beyond the "harm horizon," making shallow alignment optimal under standard RLHF objectives. Qi et al. (2024): safety removed by fine-tuning on 10 adversarial examples. Hubinger et al. (2024, Sleeper Agents): inserted backdoors persist through standard safety training, which may teach concealment rather than removal. **2026 addition:** *Teaching Claude Why* (Kutasov, Jermyn, et al., Anthropic Alignment Science, May 2026) — training on demonstrations near the eval distribution suppressed agentic misalignment without OOD generalization while masking detection; principle-carrying, structurally-different data (ethical-advice transcripts, constitution documents, admirable-AI stories) generalized strongly, with ~3M principled tokens matching ~85M scenario tokens. This is the closest published result to the framework's central bet and the direct evidence base for out-of-expertise review and the reviewer-critique data class.

**3. Shared neural substrate of failure.** Gao et al. (2025, H-Neurons): under 0.1% of neurons causally linked to hallucination, sycophancy, false-premise acceptance, and jailbreak vulnerability simultaneously; amplifying worsens all four, suppressing improves all four; the shared mechanism is over-compliance; the neurons form during pretraining (~0.97 parameter stability through alignment). The integration argument's empirical foundation: if the failures share a pretraining-formed substrate, the fix must be in the pretraining distribution.

**4. Single-component improvement degrades the whole.** OpenAI's o3 doubled hallucination on PersonQA versus o1 (33% vs 16%) — stronger reasoning without matching calibration and grounding made outcomes worse. Sharma et al. (2024): RLHF amplifies sycophancy because matching user beliefs predicts higher preference scores. Components must co-develop.

**5. Compound-concept representation.** Templeton et al. (2024): sparse autoencoders extracting up to 34M features from Claude 3 Sonnet, including unified cross-modal, cross-language concepts and abstract behavioral features; clamping features causally steers behavior. Valois et al. (2025, Frame Representation Hypothesis): multi-token words form coherent geometric structures carrying supra-token semantics. Zou et al. (2023, Representation Engineering): honesty, harmlessness, and fairness encoded as readable, controllable activation-space directions. Co-occurrence-formed compounds are real, measurable objects — the mechanism the trace specification depends on.

**The numbered reading list, mapped to components.** #1 Reinforcement Learning on Pre-Training Data and #6 RLP — the training paradigm (component 8). #2 CoT + RAG reliability and #9 hallucination mitigation — the verification reflex. #3 Enhancing LLMs through Structured Reasoning — SRP's published cousin. #4 Stress-Testing Model Specs — character differences under pressure; the eval shape for personality. #5 Mem0 — the memory-operation set (component 6). #7 Cognitive Foundations for Reasoning — the CogFound 28-element taxonomy, the external evaluation instrument (mapping table to SRP-CCC components still needed). #8 The Era of Agentic Organization — multi-agent organization, relevant to the editorial board. #10 CharacterGPT and #14 PersonaLLM — persona construction and expression precedents for archetype work. #11 Humanoid Artificial Consciousness via psychoanalysis and personality theory — archetype-depth precedent. #12 RAG for knowledge-intensive NLP — the contrast case the memory pillar defines itself against. #13 Defeating Nondeterminism in LLM Inference — evaluation reliability. Unnumbered but in scope: A-MEM (agentic memory), Checklist-Guided Memory Architectures, Context Engineering 2.0, LongRoPE (component 5), Attention Residuals, and *The Bitter Lesson* as the standing counter-argument every curation claim must answer.

**External validation instruments.** CogFound: built independently of SRP-CCC, so measurements escape self-validation contamination. DataxLLM: a 500+ reference survey independently converging on distribution-is-destiny, and the source of the novelty finding — "no SAGE equivalent in the literature." **Pending audit:** Persona Hub (Tencent, ~2024; from training knowledge, unverified) scaled synthetic data generation with ~1B shallow personas; it is adjacent enough that the novelty claim should not be repeated in public-facing material until a literature pass distinguishes SAGE's archetypal depth, shared reasoning spine, and staffed editorial layer from persona-breadth approaches.

**Theoretical defenses** (promoted from recovery files into the canonical). The **word-embedding convergence analogy** answers the inter-rater-reliability objection — enough scorers converge their variance into a unified representation, as embeddings do — with the honest caveat that it holds only if variance is noise around a shared signal, which is exactly why archetypal definition work is scoring-viability work. The **domain-mismatch defense** answers DeepSeek-R1-style objections — RL counter-evidence from binary-verification domains does not transfer to open-ended analytical targets — and is now partially *absorbed* rather than only deflected: with Coder in the Core 11, the binary-verifiable domain sits inside the architecture, anchoring grader calibration with ground truth. **Scale anchors** for small-but-curated: R1-Distill-Qwen-1.5B at 83.9% on MATH, beating GPT-4o-class models; o1 at the 89th Codeforces percentile.

## Component-to-Component Interactions

What is lost when one element is removed. **Structure × Diversity = adaptive consistency**: without Structure, diversity is chaos; without diversity, Structure is rigidity; together, a consistent process applied flexibly. **Archetype balance × SRP = intrinsic alignment**: SRP without the wisdom filter reasons competently toward arbitrary goals; the filter without SRP is "be wise" with no mechanism; together, alignment becomes intrinsic to reasoning. **Iteration × Quality control = compounding excellence**: QC alone cannot scale, iteration alone collapses; together the dataset grows in size and quality, on the invariant that accepted output beats prior average. **Tools × Memory × Reasoning = cognitive architecture** (see the tool-use section). **Compiler × Editorial board × Human audit = scalable quality assurance**: the compiler validates structure at scale; the board catches substantive failure and generates principle-carrying critique data; human audit keeps the board honest; findings feed back into compiler rules. Quality assurance learns.

## The Practical Operational Sequence

The runtime walkthrough — the *how* counterpart to the architectural *why*. The model receives the prompt; selects a Structure method from the matrix; restates the problem in its own words; decomposes (entities, relationships, hierarchies, dependencies); sets boundaries with reasons; identifies constraints (time, budget, technical, legal, ethical); surfaces assumptions and flags the fragile ones; calibrates detail; saves the structured problem space to the scratchpad; asks clarifying questions if needed. It selects a Reasoning method; develops three genuinely distinct rivals framed as testable claims; plans what evidence would support or break each and which is most discriminating; executes real tool calls; assesses each result for authority, recency, methodology, and bias with a one-to-five confidence score; extracts claims with quotes, provenance, and rival-tags; weighs support and contradiction per rival; designs discriminating tests; specifies a kill-step per rival (indicator, threshold, action, owner, timeframe); synthesizes, selects the winner with explicit justification and quantified confidence, acknowledges the losers' residual merits, and documents what would change the conclusion. It retrieves relevant long-term memory and writes new entries that pass the killer-item gate — key, value, provenance, confidence, reuse potential, expiry, tags. It selects a Presentation method fitted to audience and purpose; organizes content with priority ordering; links every claim to scratchpad evidence by reference; states numeric confidence with basis and bounds; and ends with next steps that are prioritized, owned where ownership is known, time-bound where deadlines apply, and conditional where the action depends on which scenario unfolds. Adaptive depth governs how much of this the user sees.

## Quality Gates and Failure Modes

Eight named failure modes, each with detection and mitigation. **Mode collapse**: homogenized synthetic data scoring well while losing diversity — detected by declining method-diversity and shrinking score variance; mitigated by diversity audits, fresh expert traces, forced method variety, human spot-checks. **Cosmetic rivals**: hypotheses that differ in wording, not mechanism — compiler similarity scoring plus human semantic analysis; mitigated by mechanism-extraction improvements and contrastive examples. **Simulated tool calls**: faked interactions — format and plausibility checks; verbatim-structure requirements; random verification. **Superficial archetype engagement**: traces that gesture at the profession's wisdom anatomy without depth — human audit; rubric improvement; contrastive examples. **Compiler overfitting**: the generator learns to game the checks — high pass rates with human-found misses; independent audit; adversarial testing of the compiler itself. **Training distribution drift**: category balance shifts across generations — monitoring; hard percentage constraints; rebalancing injections. **Concept-cluster fragmentation** (new): a trace names a concept without activating its dependency partners — a hollow compound that reads correctly and encodes nothing; detected with the semantic-layer toolkit (working-definition demands, dependency-partner checks); mitigated by archetype definitions that specify each profession's load-bearing compounds. **Surface-conformity review** (new): the editorial board grading format instead of stated reasons, rebuilding the *Teaching Claude Why* trap inside the factory; detected by auditing reviews for principle-explication; mitigated by the grading sheet's hard caps and by keeping review prompts why-shaped rather than checklist-shaped.

Two structural risks sit beneath the modes. The **validation gap**: structural completeness is checkable; reasoning rigor and phase-linkage quality require semantic understanding automated tools handle poorly; implicit traces are hardest, because absent structure and unlabeled structure look alike from outside. Until the compiler exists, quality rests on human review, which does not scale — the editorial-board design is the framework's answer, and it is unproven. **Inter-rater reliability**: objective dimensions are easy; subtle ones (genuine distinctness, personality coherence, calibration appropriateness) are the weakest practical link — see the word-embedding defense and its caveat; archetypal definition work is the mitigation. The **bootstrap problem** binds both: without the fixed held-out evaluation set measuring integration, improvement and mode collapse are indistinguishable.

## The Open Strategic Fork — Path A versus Path B

The framework's biggest unmade decision: how the reflex gets installed. **Path A — SRP-dominant pretraining.** Most or all pretraining data in SRP/SAGE format; smaller model and budget. The bet: a small reflexively-structured model beats a large veneer-structured one. Kill-step: if scaling laws bite and the model cannot reach baseline knowledge competence, the result is beautiful reasoning about not enough. **Path B — two-stage.** Verified broad pretraining first, then heavy SRP/CCC/SAGE mid-training. Preserves coverage. Kill-step: if late-installed reflex is a thin overlay that drops under adversarial pressure, the result is broad knowledge with a fragile reasoning shape. The choice turns on an empirical unknown — **how late a reflex can be installed and still be a reflex** — with no decisive evidence either way; note that continued training from any existing base model *is already Path B*. The **poisoning reframe** lowers Path B's cost: the verification bar on non-SRP data is not "every fact ground-truthed" but "no systematic shape-corrupting content, no reasoning-shaped errors, no trigger patterns, high care on safety and identity material" — contamination is non-linear in systematicity and shape, not in factual-error density. A related unresolved architecture question gates the encoder-decoder-versus-decoder-only decision: whether SRP-CCC trace structure can approximate multi-token planning in a decoder-only model.

## History — Six Acts and a Pivot

**Act 1 — Seeds (Apr 2023 – mid 2024).** Shapiro's heuristic imperatives plant "what character should an AI have?"; AI-therapist feasibility chats begin the Therapist thread; Horsley's *Unlimited Memory* seeds the memory pillar — and kill-steps originate there as mnemonic image-quality checks before migrating into SRP as falsification conditions; PARA lands. **Act 2 — Pillars assemble (mid 2024 – Aug 2025).** Agentic system-building muscle (solo-D&D engine, Mindcraft-adjacent work); Wave Function Collapse arrives as a procgen algorithm, later a planning metaphor; the **Mixture-of-Experts review pattern** — five expert perspectives (Systems Engineer, Psychologist/Therapist, Generalist, Memory Expert, Scientist) — emerges as the direct ancestor of the facets *and, in hindsight, of the editorial board*; the four foundational books (Horsley, Gawande, Clear, Forte) crystallize as one synthesis. **Act 3 — Convergence (Aug – Oct 2025).** The four books become one framework; WFC reframes as a prefrontal-filter planning metaphor; Mindcraft CE becomes the test bed; Mem0 and the move into academic papers; the wiki-synthesis chain assembles the raw material of the methods library. **Act 4 — Crystallization (late Oct – Nov 2025).** C-SRP appears and the C drops within days; SRP stabilizes; the SAGE name lands and the 7-facet personal version stabilizes in the 487-message SAGE Index Checklist session; CCC arrives (predecessor PCC, with its Perspective layer dropped); tiers, combinations (4,648 first appears), killer-item, CODE/PARA, and the scratchpad are all in place by late November. **Act 5 — Maturation (Dec 2025 – Mar 2026).** The work moves into Claude; structural confidence and the compositional-library framing land; the umbrella project stabilizes as IMR (Improving Model Reasoning) with SAGE as its main output; the load-bearing definitional facts land — pretraining filter not runtime evaluator; CCC scaffolding internalized to invisibility; the three runtime skills are buil