## Confidence Calibration of Major Claims

**Very high (90–95%).** Character formation through training works; a wisdom-filtered distribution creates a different optimization target than standard RLHF; methodology transfer enables efficiency gains; transparent reasoning is trainable through trace format.

**High (80–90%).** Small specialized models compete with much larger general ones in specialized domains; tool and memory integration yields a functional cognitive architecture; contextual adaptation emerges from diverse training; ~10× cost efficiency is achievable; principle-carrying data generalizes OOD where demonstrations do not (upgraded into this band by *Teaching Claude Why*).

**Moderate (65–80%).** Bootstrap cycles compound quality if validation holds; methodology generalizes across novel domains; integrated traces produce compound representations as predicted; the profession-archetype recipe regenerates everything the facet system carried (gated by the translation test); **out-of-expertise review produces principle-explication at production quality (pending pilot)**; the archetype catalog scales to hundreds without hollowing (gated by the non-knowledge-work trial).

**Speculative (40–70%).** Architectural self-optimization; a 70B SRP-CCC model reaching 75–80% of human-comparable general intelligence; long-term bootstrap stability across many generations; the jailbreak-resistance ceiling under sustained adversarial pressure.

## Known Open Questions

Empirical: minimum viable dataset size for integration effects; optimal archetype ratio in the distribution (was: facet ratio) and the priority-tier weighting for high-stakes professions; whether 50/50 explicit-implicit is the right split; how RLP-style pretraining reward integrates with editorial quality scoring; whether reflex can be installed late (the Path A/B crux); whether decoder-only architectures can approximate multi-token planning through trace structure.

Artifacts: the compiler (specified, unbuilt — a research problem, not just engineering); the fixed held-out evaluation set (critical path); the seed gold-trace dataset of 50–100 (the actual bottleneck; a November 2025 LOW-tier ShareGPT template is flagged possibly-lost); the combinations CSV validation pass (the file now exists and was counted; its content has not been re-validated); the archetype-definition template (extract from the Therapist treatment); the first archetype batch beyond the Core 11, including one deliberately non-knowledge-work profession as the hollowness trial; the CogFound-to-SRP-CCC mapping table.

Definitional: Engineer / Systems Engineer / Coder boundaries; the Researcher facet's catalog re-entry; the lost compound word; the cognitive triad's canonical name; the dependency topology of meaning; the AI-versus-human-reasoning ontology (isomorphic, functionally equivalent, or other — undefended).

Audits: the Persona Hub literature pass before any public repetition of the novelty claim; the **translation test** — re-describe one existing Therapist gold trace in the profession-archetype schema; nothing lost means the schemas are equivalent and v2's is more general, something unfittable means the facets carried irreplaceable content and both layers return (this test gates v2's full acceptance).

## What This Framework Does Not Do

It does not specify a base architecture; it works with standard transformers. It does not guarantee quantitative outcomes; the predictions are calibrated estimates from related work. It does not eliminate human judgment; the audit layer is design, not scaffold. It does not replace standard safety practice; it complements it at the substrate level. It does not claim SRP-CCC is the only valid diversity mechanism. It does not provide a runtime evaluator — balance is exhibited, not checked. It does not claim the Core 11 roster is final, and it does not claim archetype catalogs remove the need for the compiler or for human audit. And it does not work without the validation pipeline: the framework without its gates is the framework as wishful thinking.

