# WORKING DEFINITIONS REGISTER

Load-bearing vocabulary, framework-specific, never replaced by colloquial synonyms, deliberately exempt from compression. Entries marked **(v2)** are new or materially amended in this revision.

**Distribution is Destiny** — The thesis that training distribution determines model character: patterns present in training are possible at inference; patterns absent are impossible. Post-training reshapes the surface (likelihood), not the substrate (possibility).

**Alignment-as-Capability (v2)** — The strongest one-sentence form of the thesis: if the distribution is built correctly, misalignment is structurally impossible, because aligned reasoning is what the model's capability *is* rather than a constraint on it.

**Profession-Archetype (v2)** — The unit of the personality pillar: one profession given archetype-essence-first definition (essence → operational behavior → craft / zoom-in / zoom-out / interplay), generating first-person gold traces in that profession's wise voice.

**The Core 11 (v2)** — Therapist, Scientist, Philosopher, Engineer, Artist, Teacher, Comedian, Generalist, Lawyer, Systems Engineer, Coder. Dual-role: professions in the distribution *and* the editorial board (pipeline builders, graders, reviewers). "Today, so far" — extensible by decision, not by drift.

**Editorial Dual-Role (v2)** — The property that the Core 11's work products — reviews, grading decisions, pipeline reasoning — are simultaneously training data for their own trace sets. The factory documents itself as data.

**Out-of-Expertise Review (v2)** — The assignment rule placing reviewers outside their own domain so that domain shorthand cannot pass and every trace must state its reasoning at principle level. The framework's OOD-generalization mechanism.

**Reviewer-Critique Data Class (v2)** — The named class of training data consisting of the editorial board's critique dialogues: principle-explication by construction, simultaneously filter output and distribution content.

**Multiplicative Wisdom (v2, amended)** — Π(parts), not Σ(parts); any zero collapses the whole; compensation forbidden. Relocated in v2: within a profession, craft × zoom-in × zoom-out × interplay; across the distribution, enforced at editorial review rather than scored per-trace on nine dimensions.

**The Nine Archetypal Facets (v2, amended)** — Therapist, Scientist, Philosopher, Engineer, Artist, Teacher, Comedian, Generalist, Lawyer. Historically the personality dimensions of the training-data filter; in v2, ingredient vocabulary for archetype authorship and nine of the Core 11. Not deleted — repurposed.

**The Seven SAGE Facets** — The personal-practice variant (Artist/Teacher combined, no Lawyer) embedded in the "CLAUDE SAGE Thinking" preferences. A different object with a different purpose; unaffected by the v2 pivot.

**The Nine Components (v2)** — PKM, killer-item gate, SRP, Zettelkasten, LongRoPE, Mem0, the persona quality filter (archetype catalog + Core 11), RLP/RoRL, and the encoder-decoder ideal. Must co-occur in 90–100% of training data. Distinct from the nine facets; conflating the two nines is a logged error.

**RLP / RoRL (v2)** — The training paradigm commitment: the framework's components embed in *pretraining*, not fine-tuning. The 90–100% co-presence constraint is what distinguishes RLP-style integration from structured pretraining with good data sprinkled in.

**SRP** — Structure → Reasoning → Presentation. The three-phase reasoning methodology; phases not optional, order not interchangeable. Does not stand for "Structured Reasoning Process."

**CCC** — Compare → Contrast → Consensus. The synthesis layer across multiple SRP traces at MEDIUM and HIGH tiers. Scaffolding for training; internalized to invisibility at runtime.

**Structural Confidence (v2)** — Confidence derived from the geometry of cross-trace agreement under CCC — which methods converged, from how far apart — rather than from any single trace's self-report.

**Tier (LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH)** — Complexity classification set during Structure. LOW: one trace, **three rivals**, no CCC. MEDIUM: three traces, distinct Structure and Reasoning methods, full CCC. HIGH: five traces, maximum diversity, extended CCC.

**Kill-Step** — A specific, concrete, falsifiable observation or condition that would mean an approach should be abandoned. An approach with no nameable kill-step is a belief, not a hypothesis.

**Genuine vs. Cosmetic Rivals** — Rivals are genuine if an advocate of one would find the other threatening or uncomfortable; cosmetic if they differ only in wording and an advocate would shrug.

**Phase Linkage** — The requirement that every output of one SRP phase feeds the next (entities → hypotheses; boundaries → scope; fragile assumptions → first tests; source trust → confidence numbers; kill-steps → caveats; discriminating tests → next steps). Broken linkage is a critical error.

**Phase Connectivity Check** — The pre-delivery validation that the linkage chain held end to end.

**Source Trust Levels** — Strong / moderate / weak / flagged, assigned to every source during Reasoning; directly determines Presentation confidence numbers. High confidence on weak sources is an error.

**Epistemic Status Labels** — Every claim marked fact, inference, assumption, guess, or value judgment, so load-bearing granite is distinguishable from swappable scaffolding.

**Preserved Dissent** — Unresolved genuine disagreement survives into Presentation as conditional recommendations rather than a forced winner.

**Gold Trace** — A training example meeting all SRP, CCC (per tier), archetype-balance, scratchpad, and citation requirements; eligible for the distribution.

**Combinations Matrix (srp_combinations.csv) (v2, amended)** — The catalog of **4,779** validated S-R-P pairings from 27/40/36 methods. Exists as a physical artifact in `01_Areas/SAGE_Methodology/`; line count verified June 12, 2026 (4,780 including header — the header row explains the historical 4,779/4,780 drift). Pending: content validation pass.

**Scratchpad** — The transparency layer of every trace: verbatim tool calls, attributed evidence, memory operations with rationale, internal reasoning, metacognitive notes. Claims without scratchpad citation are treated as hallucinations.

**Compiler** — The automated validation gate: structural completeness, balance thresholds, CCC quality, scratchpad integrity, citation completeness. Specified; not yet built; itself a research problem (the validation gap).

**Killer-Item Test** — The dual-condition memory gate: critical AND easy to miss. Either alone fails.

**CODE** — Capture → Organize → Distill → Express; the session-level information lifecycle.

**PARA** — Projects / Areas / Resources / Archives; organization by actionability, with movement between categories as actionability changes.

**Zettelkasten** — Atomic notes, own words, densely linked; the long-timescale network whose value grows faster than its size.

**Concept (v2)** — A stable cluster of co-occurring features that activates as a unit in representational space. Not a word; not a dictionary definition.

**Compound Concept (v2, amended)** — A concept whose internal structure binds multiple concepts, through co-occurrence, into a unit carrying emergent meaning that exists in the binding and in no component alone. Forms only when components co-occur in training; the mechanism behind full-stack trace integration.

**Context Dependence (v2)** — The mechanism by which surrounding information — lexical, sentence, discourse, domain, register — selects which clusters and compounds a token activates. The selector working, as distinct from ambiguity (the selector failing).

**Working Definition (v2)** — A compound concept deliberately pinned to a scope where precision inside the scope outweighs generality outside it. Scope-bound, revisable, compound-shaping. This register is the mechanism applied to the framework itself.

**Concept-Cluster Fragmentation (v2)** — The failure mode in which a trace names a concept without activating its dependency partners, producing a hollow compound that reads correctly and encodes nothing. Detected with the semantic-layer toolkit; a canonical quality gate as of v2.

**Adaptive Depth** — Matching the visibility of SRP structure to task complexity: light touch / visible structure / full walkthrough. Structure always runs; visibility flexes.

**50/50 Explicit-Implicit Split** — Half of gold traces visibly tag their structure; half achieve identical rigor in unlabeled prose. Implicit means unlabeled structure, never absent structure.

**Bare-Bones Sequence** — The step-by-step runtime walkthrough (the *how*), distinct from the architectural specification (the *why*).

**Path A / Path B (v2)** — The open strategic fork: SRP-dominant pretraining versus two-stage installation (broad pretraining, then heavy SRP mid-training). Turns on how late a reflex can be installed and still be a reflex.

**SAGE** — The brand name for the whole framework: thesis, methodology, architecture, practices, and the body of work. Not an acronym — neither facet set spells it.

